# '[T]' is written form for 'List<T>' and '{K: V}' for 'Hash<K, V>' -- record
# 0022, the same decision that makes 'T[]' an 'Array<T>' -- and the golden
# below is the tree after the pass, so all three read as the classes they are.
#
# Neither was lowered until 2026-09-10. They built a structural type of their
# own instead, so 'let l : [i32]' compiled and then answered to no method at
# all, while 'let l : List<i32>' worked: the sugar reached the literal and not
# the annotation. One rewrite serves the three of them now, which is why the
# nesting below is written every way round.
def takes : void
    @xs : [i32]
    @pairs : {i32: f64}
    @nested : [[i32]]
    @mixed : {i32: [f64]}
    @grid : {i32: f64}[]
    pass

class Holder:
    numbers : [i32]
    counts : {String: i32}
    fixed : f64[2]

def main : i32
    let l : [i32]
    let h : {i32: f64}
    let deep : [{i32: f64}]

    return 0
